.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1047 AM PDT Fri Oct 2 2026

VFR conditions returning to the region with the exception of HAF
where LIFR persists. Onshore winds are forecast to increase this
afternoon, yet will be weaker than previous days as high pressure
builds over the region. Expecting SCT/BKN high clouds through much
of the day today with them moving east of the region tomorrow.
Winds ease late this evening with sub-IFR conditions most likely
along the coast and around the Monterey Bay terminals late tonight
into early tomorrow morning.

Vicinity of SFO...VFR. Onshore winds will increase this afternoon
between 21Z-00Z. Winds ease late in the evening with a 10-20%
probability of sub-MVFR (as low as LIFR) between 10Z-16Z Saturday
based off of the NBM. Thus, have left ceilings/fog out of the
forecast for both SFO and OAK.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...VFR. Generally light onshore winds will
increase this afternoon before easing after sunset. Moderate
confidence for sub-MVFR and as low as LIFR conditions to return
overnight, generally a 40-55% probability from 02Z-15Z Saturday.
Any low clouds and fog that develops will dissipate between
15Z-18Z.

