.FIRE WEATHER...
Issued at 353 AM PDT Fri Oct 2 2026

Ridging will lead to hot and dry conditions across the region
through the seven day outlook. Daytime humidity retention will
remain poor to very poor away from the immediate coast, while
overnight, the thermal belts remain active and humidity retention
in the higher elevations is poor. Pushes of offshore flow are
possible in the higher elevations each morning. Hazardous heat
builds this weekend, particularly impacting fire crews across the
interior mountains and the Santa Lucia range.

